2 CONC ul. Persons who wished to obtain salvation also sent in information, showing how on the mother's side they came from a salvation family, such as a Nils Larsson, granddaughter of Knut Ulfsson (Soop) of Malmö. However, Rasmus has no
2 CONC t been without help in his genealogical research. The other chancellery clerks, especially Hans Eriksson, favored by his marriage, apparently helped him, and towards the end of his life Peder Mansson Utter also appeared. - Rasmus 
2 CONC never prepared an entire family book, but one of his later assistants seems to have brought together most of what Rasmus had written in the matter of genealogies, and this is preserved in two copies, one, the so-called Per Brahe's
2 CONC  family book in Kungl. The library Rälambska collection, the other in the National Archives in the Skokloster collection. Rasmus's work was continued by the above-mentioned Peder Mänsson Utter, who was far more critically inclined
2 CONC  than Rasmus. In his Collectanea, he has indeed published a Genealogy, entirely based on Rasmus's researches, but he has attached to it a large number of letter extracts to confirm its information and here and there, with the guid
2 CONC ance of the records, established new genealogies. This collection is stored in the National Archives. Available in Uppsala library there is a book of arms by him, As is well known, Messenins in his Theatrum nobilitatis left the fi
2 CONC rst printed family book. For the most part, it is based on Rasmus Ludvigsson's family record, but contains a lot of puppets, which are not found there, and for which one can assume now-lost sources. The family book, however, suffe
2 CONC rs from the major fault that no evidence for its information is ever presented. Bure's much-discussed family book is only a compilation of Rasmus Ludvigsson's, Utter's and Messenü's works. After Rasmus Ludvigsson, hardly anyone ha
2 CONC s enjoyed a greater reputation as a genealogical researcher than Peringsköld. In his Biographica illustrium virorum oh Characteras procerum
