1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/M%C3%B6rner_af_Tuna_nr_109 '''Christina Maria Mörner af Tuna'''], född 1653-06-23 på Mörnersholm (1). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1680-09-29''' med sin syssling, generalmajoren [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ribbing_nr_15#TAB_26 '''Johan Ribbing'''], i hans 2:a gifte
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1700''' (2).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Depending on sources, Mörnerholm or Mörnersholm is located where Nevanlinna (Neovia) used to be located, which is the current day St. Petersburg, Russia. Her father was a governor general over there at the time of her birth.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Given her death in 1700, and the fact that she died the same year as her husband at the onset of the great Northern War, chances are that she died in battle of Riga, which was the strongest Swedish garrison in Livonia at the ti
2 CONC me. Her following her husband to the battlefield in Narva, where he died, doesn't seem likely. 
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
