1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sven Jonson Västgöte=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Vadstena Castle (Swedish: Vadstena slott) is a former Royal Castle in Vadstena, the province of Östergötland, Sweden.
2 CONT * Sven Västgöte's house in the 1600s. He is the  oldest known owner of the commercial estate is Sven Jönsson Västgöte, commander at Vadstena Castle. 1642 After Sven Jönsson's death, the farm is sold to the well-known merchant and 
2 CONC mayor Erland Svensson, who already lived in the farm. Vadstena Castle was built by King Gustav I in 1545 on lake Vattern in Sweden. It was meant to protect Stockholm from enemies approaching from the south. The original ramparts w
2 CONC ere torn down in the 19th century. Interestingly, the present-day ones were reconstructed only in 1999 - it was the result of 140 years of debate that began immediately after they were demolished, when the soil masses were needed 
2 CONC as backfill for the new harbor pier. The castle is deemed one of Sweden's best examples of Renaissance architecture. One of the first opera performance was staged within its walls.
2 CONT
