1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Petrus Paulinus Hilletan=
2 CONT
2 CONT The family has a common origin with the noble families Lilliengrip , and Lillienstam
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Paulus Erici Wirestadius and Anna Pedersdotter 
2 CONT * Lived on his own a farm in Lihult
2 CONT * Parish priest in Hinneryd, Växjö
2 CONT * Death: June 14, 1669 in Hinneryd (G), Småland, Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Hilletan_nr_1022 Noble family Hilletan no. 1022, by Adelsvapen Genealogies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Petrus Paulinus''' (son of Paulus Erici, Tab. 1), vicar of Hinneryd in 1634 1 . Lived on his own farm Lihult. Died 1669 before 14/6. '''Married to Botilda Jonsdotter , who was still alive in 1671, daughter of the bailiff at Tof
2 CONC taholm Jöns Joensson (brother of lieutenant colonel Peder Joensson, knighted Gyllensvärd ).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Paul Paulin,'''  Provincial Inspector. Customs inspector in Hälsingborg. Provincial inspector first in Gothenburg, then in Riga. Children: Paul Paulin , noble Lillienstam, died 1731. See noble family Lillienstam .
2 CONT * '''Carl Paulin,''' knighted Lilliengrip . ennobled Lilliengrip (son of Petrus Paulinus, see noble family Hilletan. Customs officer in Malmö. Commissioner in Färs and Frosta districts of Landskrona county in 1677. Inspector at th
2 CONC e alum mill in Skåne. District chief in Ingelstads, Herrestads, Färs and Frosta districts in 1689. Knighted 1690-09-10 (introduced in 1693 under no. 1212). Lived in 1697, but was dead before 1702-11-12. 'During the Malmö siege and
2 CONC  storming by the Danes in 1677, he, along with other civilians, took up arms and was entrusted with the bastion at Syndre port, which he bravely defended with seven cannons, a cadet constable and two soldiers. Often participated i
2 CONC n parties against the Snapphans and the rebellious common people in Skåne and made considerable advances to the crown from their own funds.' Married to Eleonora NN, born 1644, died 1716 and buried 1716-03-03 in Alingsås. 
2 CONT * '''Magnus Paulin ,''' county governor in Luggude and Bjäre counties in Skåne, mayor, g. l:o m. Ottiliana Rasmusdotter Rafn.
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Paulin , b.''' 1645, † 1721, married to Abrahamus Jonce Lannerus, adl. the Lannerstierna family , b. 1638, † 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT
